{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NyPV68u3eFB8Xi8FS7LsAh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# edge_detector\n2\t\n3\tDetects rising and falling edges of an asynchronous input after synchronizing it into the\n4\t`clk` domain with a 2-flop synchronizer.\n5\t\n6\t## Ports\n7\t| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n8\t|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n9\t| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n10\t| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n11\t| din   | in  | 1     | Asynchronous input |\n12\t| rise  | out | 1     | One-cycle pulse on a synchronized 0 -> 1 transition |\n13\t| fall  | out | 1     | One-cycle pulse on a synchronized 1 -> 0 transition |\n14\t| any   | out | 1     | One-cycle pulse on either transition |\n15\t\n16\t## Structure / timing (normative)\n17\t- Three registers, **all reset to 0** while `rst_n` is low, all updated on every rising edge of `clk`:\n18\t  - `sync1 <= din`\n19\t  - `sync2 <= sync1`   (`sync2` is the synchronized version of `din`)\n20\t  - `prev  <= sync2`   (`sync2` delayed one cycle)\n21\t- Outputs are combinational functions of `sync2` and `prev`:\n22\t  - `rise = sync2 & ~prev`\n23\t  - `fall = ~sync2 & prev`\n24\t  - `any  = sync2 ^ prev`\n25\t- Consequently, if `din` changes and is stable across rising edges, it is captured into `sync1`\n26\t  at edge k, into `sync2` at edge k+1, and the corresponding pulse is high from edge k+1 until\n27\t  edge k+2 (exactly one clock cycle).\n28\t- Immediately after reset (all registers 0) no output pulses until `din` has been\n29\t  synchronized; e.g. if `din` stays 0 through and after reset, `rise`, `fall` and `any` stay 0.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b366691b-e39e-4426-b0ec-a6be6755d7a8","uuid":"734389f7-3123-41f9-86de-e3ea329ac61e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:39:27.825Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\abhig\\Documents\\New folder\\assay\\runs\\v2__edge_detector__t1\\workspace\\spec.md","content":"# edge_detector\n\nDetects rising and falling edges of an asynchronous input after synchronizing it into the\n`clk` domain with a 2-flop synchronizer.\n\n## Ports\n| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n| din   | in  | 1     | Asynchronous input |\n| rise  | out | 1     | One-cycle pulse on a synchronized 0 -> 1 transition |\n| fall  | out | 1     | One-cycle pulse on a synchronized 1 -> 0 transition |\n| any   | out | 1     | One-cycle pulse on either transition |\n\n## Structure / timing (normative)\n- Three registers, **all reset to 0** while `rst_n` is low, all updated on every rising edge of `clk`:\n  - `sync1 <= din`\n  - `sync2 <= sync1`   (`sync2` is the synchronized version of `din`)\n  - `prev  <= sync2`   (`sync2` delayed one cycle)\n- Outputs are combinational functions of `sync2` and `prev`:\n  - `rise = sync2 & ~prev`\n  - `fall = ~sync2 & prev`\n  - `any  = sync2 ^ prev`\n- Consequently, if `din` changes and is stable across rising edges, it is captured into `sync1`\n  at edge k, into `sync2` at edge k+1, and the corresponding pulse is high from edge k+1 until\n  edge k+2 (exactly one clock cycle).\n- Immediately after reset (all registers 0) no output pulses until `din` has been\n  synchronized; e.g. if `din` stays 0 through and after reset, `rise`, `fall` and `any` stay 0.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
